# Tree Rings Counter — Project Context

Cross-platform mobile/web app (iOS, Android, Web) that estimates a tree's age from a photo of its cut cross-section by counting annual growth rings with AI.

## Current state (as of March 2026)

All code is written and dependencies installed. The app has been run locally for the first time (March 9, 2026).

**Setup is complete:**
- Project moved to `C:\dev\tree-rings-counter` (avoids Google Drive TAR_ENTRY_ERROR)
- `cd app && npm install` ✅ — Expo SDK 53, expo-router v5, all packages at correct versions
- `cd backend && pip install -r requirements.txt` ✅ — FastAPI, OpenCV, `google-genai`, OpenAI SDK
- `backend/.env` has `GEMINI_API_KEY` filled in ✅
- Migrated from deprecated `google-generativeai` → `google-genai` SDK ✅

**To run:**
```bash
# Backend (from backend/)
uvicorn main:app --reload

# Frontend (from app/)
npx expo start   # w=browser, scan QR for Expo Go
```

Phase 2 (YOLO26 fine-tuning) has not been done yet — `USE_YOLO=false` in `.env` keeps it on the LLM path.

## Project structure

```
tree-rings-counter/
├── app/          # Expo app (iOS + Android + Web)
└── backend/      # FastAPI backend + ML pipeline
```

## Stack

| Layer | Technology | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Mobile/Web | React Native + Expo SDK 53, Expo Router v4, TypeScript | Single codebase for all platforms |
| Styling | NativeWind v4 + Tailwind CSS v3 | v3 only — NativeWind v5 (Tailwind v4) in development |
| Backend | FastAPI (Python 3.12) | `backend/main.py` |
| Phase 1 AI | Gemini 2.5 Flash (primary) + GPT-4o (fallback) | `backend/ml/llm_vision.py` — uses `google-genai` SDK (`client.aio.models.generate_content`) |
| Phase 2 AI | YOLO26-seg fine-tuned on tree rings | `backend/ml/yolo_inference.py` |
| Mobile builds | Expo EAS Build | `app/eas.json` |
| Web hosting | Vercel | `expo export --platform web` |
| Backend hosting | Render | `backend/render.yaml` |

## Key design decisions

- **Poláček 2023 Mask R-CNN**: NOT used as-is — trained on microscope images, ~18 min/image. Use its Zenodo dataset for YOLO26 fine-tuning only.
- **YOLO26-seg over YOLO11/v8**: Released Jan 14 2026, NMS-free, 43% faster CPU inference, same Ultralytics API (`from ultralytics import YOLO`).
- **Gemini 2.5 Flash over GPT-4o**: Primary (cost/speed); GPT-4o fallback when confidence < `FALLBACK_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD`.
- **Render over Railway**: Better free tier RAM for ML inference (750 hr/month always-on).
- **`@/` path alias**: Configured in `tsconfig.json` + `babel.config.js` via `babel-plugin-module-resolver`.

## Frontend key files

- `app/app/_layout.tsx` — Expo Router root layout, dark forest-green theme
- `app/app/index.tsx` — home screen, triggers photo capture + calls `analyzeImage()`
- `app/app/result/[id].tsx` — result screen: photo, SVG ring overlay, age card, share button
- `app/components/CameraCapture.tsx` — camera viewfinder with concentric circle guidance overlay + gallery picker
- `app/components/RingOverlay.tsx` — SVG cross-section with proportional concentric rings
- `app/components/ResultCard.tsx` — age estimate, confidence badge, model used, AI notes
- `app/services/api.ts` — `analyzeImage(uri)` → `POST /analyze` → `AnalysisResult`

## Backend key files

- `backend/routers/analyze.py` — `POST /analyze`: validates upload, preprocesses, routes to LLM or YOLO
- `backend/ml/preprocess.py` — CLAHE contrast enhancement + Hough circle crop + 1024×1024 resize
- `backend/ml/llm_vision.py` — Gemini 2.5 Flash primary, GPT-4o fallback, returns structured JSON
- `backend/ml/yolo_inference.py` — YOLO26-seg Phase 2 (activated by `USE_YOLO=true` in `.env`)
- `backend/ml/training/train_yolo26.py` — fine-tuning script
- `backend/ml/training/convert_polacek_to_yolo.py` — converts Poláček CVAT annotations → YOLO format

## Environment variables (`backend/.env`)

```
GEMINI_API_KEY=        # required — from aistudio.google.com
OPENAI_API_KEY=        # optional — GPT-4o fallback
PRIMARY_MODEL=gemini
FALLBACK_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD=0.5
USE_YOLO=false         # set true + YOLO_WEIGHTS_PATH for Phase 2
YOLO_WEIGHTS_PATH=ml/weights/yolo26n-seg-tree-rings.pt
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:8081,...
```

## Phase 2 YOLO training (when ready)

1. Download Poláček dataset: https://zenodo.org/record/8428752
2. Convert annotations: `python backend/ml/training/convert_polacek_to_yolo.py --cvat_xml ... --images_dir ... --output_dir data/train`
3. Train: `python backend/ml/training/train_yolo26.py`
4. Set `USE_YOLO=true` and `YOLO_WEIGHTS_PATH=ml/weights/.../best.pt` in `backend/.env`
